Speaker diarization helper (recorder/diar/, tractus-diar; optional)
--------------------------------------------------------------

The helper is a separate Swift package built from source by the user
(see recorder/README.md). With the
default `--diarizer auto` it runs only when Nemotron used all 8 speaker
channels; `tractus transcribe --diarizer fluid` runs it always.

8. FluidAudio v0.17.5 (Swift package, commit 0b1f46289fe27d95b5e66ad8be46e64f5ee02ae7)
   https://github.com/FluidInference/FluidAudio
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Includes fastcluster (C++, centroid linkage), https://github.com/fastcluster/fastcluster
   © 2011 Daniel Müllner, © Google Inc., BSD 2-Clause License.
   Includes a VBx clustering implementation (BUT Speech@FIT),
   https://github.com/BUTSpeechFIT/VBx, Apache License 2.0.
   The NeMo text-normalization binary of FluidAudio is not linked
   (package traits disabled). The TTS lexicon resource bundle that
   SwiftPM places next to the executable is not used by tractus-diar
   and should not be shipped with it.

